### Task Management API requests
###
### Open this file in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client)
### and click "Send Request" above any request. JetBrains IDEs run it natively.
###
### Start the API first: docker compose up --build
### A fresh database has three demo tasks (IDs 1, 2, and 3).
### Run the requests in order: the create request saves the new task ID for later ones.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### Create
### ---------------------------------------------------------------

### Create a task -> 201 Created with a Location header
# @name createTask
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Write a smoke test",
  "description": "Check the local task API.",
  "status": "pending",
  "assignee": "Alex",
  "dueDate": "2030-02-01"
}

### Remember the new task ID for the requests below
@taskId = {{createTask.response.body.$.id}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### Read
### ---------------------------------------------------------------

### List the first page (default page size is 20) -> 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks

### Filter by status and assignee, one task per page -> 200 OK
# Both filters are exact, case-sensitive matches. Status is pending, inProgress, or done.
# @name firstPage
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks?status=pending&assignee=Alex&pageSize=1

### Next page: pass nextAfterId from the previous response as afterId with the same filters
# A null nextAfterId means there are no more matching tasks.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks?status=pending&assignee=Alex&pageSize=1&afterId={{firstPage.response.body.$.nextAfterId}}

### Get the task created above -> 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks/{{taskId}}

### Get a demo task -> 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks/1

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### Update (PUT replaces the whole task, so send all five fields)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------

### Replace the task created above -> 200 OK
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks/{{taskId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Write a smoke test",
  "description": "Checked against the local task API.",
  "status": "inProgress",
  "assignee": "Morgan",
  "dueDate": "2030-03-15"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### Delete
### ---------------------------------------------------------------

### Delete the task created above -> 204 No Content
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks/{{taskId}}

### Get the deleted task -> 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks/{{taskId}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### Error responses (application/problem+json)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------

### Missing required fields and an invalid status -> 400 Bad Request with field errors
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "   ",
  "status": "blocked"
}

### Blank assignee -> 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Valid title",
  "description": "Valid description.",
  "status": "pending",
  "assignee": " ",
  "dueDate": "2030-02-01"
}

### Invalid date format -> 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Valid title",
  "description": "Valid description.",
  "status": "pending",
  "assignee": "Alex",
  "dueDate": "01/02/2030"
}

### Invalid filter status -> 400 Bad Request
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks?status=blocked

### Page size out of range (1 to 100) -> 400 Bad Request
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks?pageSize=101

### ID must be a positive integer -> 400 Bad Request
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks/0

### Valid ID with no matching task -> 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks/999999

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### API documentation
### ---------------------------------------------------------------

### OpenAPI document -> 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi/v1.json

### Interactive Scalar reference (open http://localhost:8080/scalar/v1 in a browser)
GET {{baseUrl}}/scalar/v1
